    {
      "id": "03-fats",
      "index": 2,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "fats",
      "text": "37.1 grams of fat. The good part is 5.8 grams of polyunsaturated fat. The bad part is 12.6 grams of saturated fat. For meat, that saturated fat is the main tradeoff.",
      "textSha256": "f1e436044c7a885f8238d4802578529ada5ad65417d08b9d5b5f00ac19f0bbd1",
      "characterCount": 165,
      "byteLength": 197320,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/bacon/voice-v13-blocks/03-fats.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "MoLLJ7UR8UoryF6E4kPp",
        "historyItemId": "3FqNzePQvm3CzR31FxGD"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/bacon/voice/voice-v13-blocks/03-fats.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-carbs",
      "index": 3,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "carbs",
      "text": "Carbs are basically irrelevant here. There are no defensible carb submacros to score. For plain cured meat, that is normal, so this section mostly stays out of the way.",
      "textSha256": "57a574d5dac475f2905e12b0ce84e4f1a8a9188fa91a1d0bff68551c24797176",
      "characterCount": 168,
      "byteLength": 144657,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/bacon/voice-v13-blocks/04-carbs.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "rEw2tEt1Wc45C4Afo0lq",
        "historyItemId": "xfGdXbpWPLYAWceeakHc"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/bacon/voice/voice-v13-blocks/04-carbs.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-proteins",
      "index": 4,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "proteins",
      "text": "13.7 grams of protein. Essential amino acids are 9 out of 9, and non-essential amino acids are 10 out of 11. Collagen is only 0.4 grams. For meat, the protein quality is the main upside.",
      "textSha256": "7fb80e2741ca3df16714eca2464cd17103a7981e729af0cf1bdbcaaaf9e49672",
      "characterCount": 186,
      "byteLength": 234519,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/bacon/voice-v13-blocks/05-proteins.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "JFjPx52k2h0QGUnBSR5h",
        "historyItemId": "2raJv7zixbWB7gRU1hK8"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/bacon/voice/voice-v13-blocks/05-proteins.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-vitamins",
      "index": 5,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "vitamins",
      "text": "Vitamin B12 is the clear mark at 21% daily value. Vitamin D is only 1% daily value. For meat, this is useful B12 support, not a broad vitamin profile.",
      "textSha256": "b182a3cfdf3d80d7f840cc51ec5887fd638b1193fe7ce7061bbb20a19a0e36e8",
      "characterCount": 150,
      "byteLength": 178512,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/bacon/voice-v13-blocks/06-vitamins.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "ypj0tDco0tOZIxqFffQM",
        "historyItemId": "i9irME5bV8fgnvf0oSc1"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/bacon/voice/voice-v13-blocks/06-vitamins.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-minerals",
      "index": 6,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "minerals",
      "text": "Zinc is the best mineral at 10% daily value. Iron is only 2% daily value, and potassium is 4% daily value. For meat, the mineral section is mostly weak.",
      "textSha256": "4e37a71f6ca5c551e6e9346a9673c682d8778a55b3c3ad2b3cc4f52719453e0d",
      "characterCount": 152,
      "byteLength": 178512,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/bacon/voice-v13-blocks/07-minerals.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "rbZM0COnphLaqpA4jNNf",
        "historyItemId": "BSFzWObapN3tuCrwEXOi"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/bacon/voice/voice-v13-blocks/07-minerals.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-pros",
      "index": 7,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "pros",
      "text": "Pros first: very tasty. Small amounts add a lot of flavour. It works well as a topper or side. The comfort-food appeal is obvious.",
      "textSha256": "43a0f738943669b170e32c8ef7d18d46b481066ed54b257b320f69916ac00112",
      "characterCount": 130,
      "byteLength": 153435,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/bacon/voice-v13-blocks/08-pros.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "cl2iseUXTiNKjzexbe7c",
        "historyItemId": "B4n6SSZyv7qU9vesN5E9"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/bacon/voice/voice-v13-blocks/08-pros.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-cons",
      "index": 8,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "cons",
      "text": "Cons next: sodium is high. Processing is the bigger health tradeoff. The salty, fatty flavour also makes portions easy to overdo, so bacon works best as a small add-on.",
      "textSha256": "613cadc9392be9920b1d46b80c3e898c663991246ad0854ca6cf2807edf51120",
      "characterCount": 168,
      "byteLength": 195648,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/bacon/voice-v13-blocks/09-cons.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "6brBsVhywfvwBeYgzKnu",
        "historyItemId": "C1xI7jGgUzmFlWvwKTvZ"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/bacon/voice/voice-v13-blocks/09-cons.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-closing_summary",
      "index": 9,
      "kind": "closing_summary",
      "sectionKey": null,
      "text": "Best bits are protein quality, vitamin B12, and strong flavour. Weak spots are saturated fat, sodium, processing, and easy portion creep. Best as a small flavour add-on, not an everyday main protein.",
      "textSha256": "b273e97bc63838aa3b8d89d5bcb8716317ee4338384e91a09d5eeb9a96e234f4",
      "characterCount": 199,
      "byteLength": 226995,
